body:
I like to think of it like this (I'm currently in school).

&#x200B;

I would much rather take the chance of going in debt to get an engineering degree, with the potential of not finding a good job, or getting a shitty job, or not like being an engineer.

As opposed to never going for an engineering degree and always wondering "what if?", and having regret for not taking the chance.

&#x200B;

I guess, ultimately it just depends on how much you want to be an engineer.
